<h1>How to Check a Job Notification</h1>
<p>Before applying for a job, carefully read the official notification. It helps you understand eligibility, deadlines, documents and the selection process.</p>

<h2>1. Verify the Official Website</h2>
<p>Find the recruitment notice on the employer's official website. For government vacancies, use the relevant official government department or recruitment portal.</p>

<h2>2. Check Eligibility</h2>
<ul>
<li>Required educational qualification</li>
<li>Minimum and maximum age</li>
<li>Nationality or domicile conditions, if applicable</li>
<li>Required registration, licence or experience</li>
<li>Category-based age relaxation, where applicable</li>
</ul>

<h2>3. Check Important Dates</h2>
<p>Note the application opening date, closing date, fee payment deadline, examination date and admit-card updates. Dates can change, so check official notices regularly.</p>

<h2>4. Understand Salary and Fees</h2>
<p>Read the pay scale, salary structure, allowances and application fee carefully. Check whether any fee exemptions apply to you.</p>

<h2>5. Understand Selection Stages</h2>
<p>The process may include a written examination, skill test, interview, document verification or medical examination. Follow the exact requirements in the notification.</p>

<h2>6. Prepare Required Documents</h2>
<ul>
<li>Educational certificates and marksheets</li>
<li>Identity proof</li>
<li>Recent photograph and signature</li>
<li>Category or domicile certificate, if required</li>
<li>Professional registration or experience proof, if required</li>
</ul>

<h2>7. Avoid Fake Vacancies</h2>
<p>Be cautious of unofficial messages, guaranteed-selection promises and requests for money to secure a job. Verify contact details and payment instructions on the official website.</p>

<h2>Before Applying</h2>
<p>Save a copy of the notification, confirm that you meet all requirements and submit the form before the deadline.</p>

